ent": "secondary_8", "type": "objective"}]}, {"responses": [{"selected": 0, "id": 0, "correct": 0, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}]}, {"selected": 0, "id": 1, "correct": 1, "_data": [{"content": "burn", "type": "text"}]}], "id": 2, "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "engenn9le06ob01re6aud03", "type": "audio"}, {"content": "If you leave a job you should be professional and not ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "incorrect", "contents": [{"content": "turn ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "post_question", "contents": {"content": "bridges.    ", "type": ""}}, {"content": "secondary_8", "type": "objective"}]}], "stimuli_ids": [], "id": 9, "template_override": 1}, {"_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": []}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Quiz", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}], "type": "RSLT", "questions": [{"responses": [{"selected": 0, "id": 0, "correct": 0, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}]}, {"selected": 0, "id": 1, "correct": 1, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}]}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}]}]}], "stimuli_ids": [], "id": 10, "template_override": 1}, {"_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " \nResearch some apps that are useful.\n", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Take Away", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Speaking", "type": "skill"}]}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "\nInstructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self Assessment.\n", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "DWS", "questions": [{"responses": [{"selected": 0, "id": 0, "correct": 1, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}]}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "engenn9le06ob01re7pdf01.pdf", "type": "pdf"}]}]}], "stimuli_ids": [], "id": 11, "template_override": 1}], "type": "scholar", "stimuli": [{"id": 0, "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}]}, {"type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "template_override": 1, "title": "", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"text": "", "image": "engenn9le06ob01re2img05.jpg", "time": "0", "id": 0}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: Hey Bianca. The job that I applied to was given to the other candidate.\n<br><span class=\"strong\">Bianca</span>: Aww, that's too bad. What's next?\n<br><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: I'll send them an email that thanks them for their time  and  confirming that I'm interested in other opportunities which may come up.\n<br><span class=\"strong\">Bianca</span>: Good idea. Friendly communication that is positive and helpful is preferable. Don't burn any bridges! Maybe you should call them. A phone call is  more personal.", "image": "engenn9le06ob01re2img05.jpg", "time": "100", "id": 1}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: Yeah, you're right. One thing I need to do is to show interest in what the company does instead of just asking for a job.\n<br><span class=\"strong\">Bianca</span>: That's important. What's the plan now?\n<br><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: Well, jobs that I am qualified for are the ones I need to focus on. And I need to get more methodical about it.\n<br><span class=\"strong\">Bianca</span>: How?", "image": "engenn9le06ob01re2img06.jpg", "time": "28000", "id": 2}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: I heard that it's really instrumental to a job search to keep track of what you do during your search. I've found an app which will help me organize potential employers who I have applied to. It's a simple organization system and it's saved on your phone. Contacts that you meet are added. When you apply for a job, the date is added. Everything is updated automatically. Most jobs are advertised online so they can be saved directly to the app.\n<br><span class=\"strong\">Bianca</span>: Wow, that sounds handy. It's important to keep a record of the people who you sent resumes to, so you can follow up with them. You need to remind the employers that you are still keen on the position and the company.\n<br><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: Yeah! And the position that I'm going to send an application to today will be the first entry in my new organization tool!", "image": "engenn9le06ob01re2img07.jpg", "time": "48000", "id": 3}], "coverimg": "engenn9le06ob01re2img05.jpg", "audiosrc": "engenn9le06ob01re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}]}]}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "The Job Search", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "The Workforce", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 1, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 6, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Identify and describe jobs and careers in both work and social contexts appropriate for the interlocutor.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Subject and Object Relative Clauses", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you want to clarify which person or thing you are talking about, you use a relative clause. We use relative clauses to give additional information about something without starting a new sentence.<br><br/>You can begin a relative clause with <span class=\"italic\">who</span> for people, <span class=\"italic\">which</span> for things or <span class=\"italic\">that</span> for either people or things.<br/>In spoken English you usually use <span class=\"italic\">that</span>, rather than <span class=\"italic\">which</span> or <span class=\"italic\">who</span>.<br/><br>You put the relative clause immediately after the noun it talks about.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "The relative clause can come after the subject or the object of the sentence. We can't drop the relative pronoun (<span class=\"italic\">that, who, which</span>).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "A <span class=\"strong\">subject relative clause</span> describes the subject of the clause and comes after the subject of the sentence.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example: <br><span class=\"italic\">The job that I applied to was given to the other candidate.<br/>Which job? The job that I applied to.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The clause <span class=\"italic\">that I applied to</span> immediately follows <span class=\"italic\">job</span> - the noun it describes.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "An <span class=\"strong\">object relative clause </span>describes the object of the clause and comes after the object of the sentence.<br>For example:<br><span class=\"italic\"> I'm interested in any other opportunities which may come up.</span><br/>Which opportunities? The opportunities which may come up.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Clause\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Relative connector\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Type of Relative  Clause\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Friendly communication that is positive and helpful is preferable.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"that is positive and helpful\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"that\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"subject\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'm interested in any other opportunities which may come up.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"which may come up.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"which\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"object\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">It's important to keep a record of the people who you sent r\u00e9sum\u00e9s to . \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"who you sent resumes to.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"who\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"object\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "I've found an app <span class=\"strong\">which</span> will help me organize potential employers who I have applied to.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The position<span class=\"strong\"> that </span>I'm going to send an application to today will be the first entry in my new organization tool!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The job<span class=\"strong\"> that</span> I applied to was given to the other candidate. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I'll send them an email <span class=\"strong\">that </span>thanks them for their time.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " The Simple Present Passive", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use an active structure when you want the <span class=\"italic\">'doer'</span> of the action to be the subject.<br>You use a passive structure when you want the <span class=\"italic\">'receiver'</span> of the action to be the subject. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "In <span class=\"strong\">Active</span> sentences, the thing doing the action is the subject of the sentence and the thing receiving the action is the object. Most sentences are active.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "[Thing doing action] + [verb] + [thing receiving action]", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:<br>Active sentence = <span class=\"italic\"> Employers</span>(subject)<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">  advertise </span>most jobs</span> (object) <span class=\"italic\">online</span>.</span> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "In <span class=\"strong\"> Passive </span>sentences, the thing receiving the action is the subject of the sentence and the thing doing the action is optionally included near the end of the sentence. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use the passive form if you think that the thing receiving the action is more important or should be emphasized. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can also use the passive form if you do not know who is doing the action or if you do not want to mention who is doing the action.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "[Thing receiving action] + [be] + [past participle of verb] + [by] + [thing doing action]", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:<br> Passive sentence = <span class=\"italic\">Most jobs </span>(subject)<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\"> are advertised</span> online.</span> (by employers)</span><br>  It is not necessary to mention the object in a passive sentence. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You make the Present Passive form of a verb by using tenses of the<span class=\"strong\"> be </span>verb followed by the past participle. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The Simple Present passive form is:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Subject + am/are/is + past participle", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example: <br><span class=\"italic\">The app<span class=\"strong\"> is saved</span> on your phone.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The app is saved on your phone.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "When you apply for a job, the date is added.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Everything is updated automatically.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Most jobs are advertised online.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Jobs can be saved directly to the app.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "methodical ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "doing something carefully and using an ordered system ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I need to get more methodical about it.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le06ob01aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about events and experiences related to a job search.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "instrumental", "type": "name"}, {"content": " being important in making something happen ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": " (adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I heard that it's really instrumental to a job search to keep track of what you do.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le06ob01aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "handy", "type": "name"}, {"content": "near and easy to use  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": " (adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: That sounds handy.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le06ob01aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to burn bridges ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to act unpleasantly in a situation that you are leaving, ensuring that you'll never be welcome to return ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Don't burn any bridges!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le06ob01aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "qualified ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "having suitable knowledge, experience, or skills, especially for a particular job ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Jobs that I am qualified for are the ones I need to focus on.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le06ob01aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "keen ", "type": "name"}, {"content": " eager to do something or wanting something to happen very much ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You need to remind employers that you are still keen on the position and the company.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le06ob01aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn9le06ob01re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Using your phone or computer, search for some apps that you think might help you search for a job and find a job.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Choose 3 apps and write a short summary of each.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Describe what the app does and why you chose it. Be sure to include how it will help you.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Present your apps to your class or group.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I talk about general issues related to a job search.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I do research online.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write a summary of my research.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I present my summaries to a group.", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "sena"}